<h1>Preferences - Display - Dimensions</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">The options in this group are related to <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Dimensioning</i></span> and <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Gap and Flush</i></span> modes.</p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="../images/preferences_dimensions.gif" width="593px" height="367px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="sub-head">Preview group</p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">Contains preview screen where all changes to the settings of the dimensions are updated.</p>
<p class="sub-head">Colouring group</p>
<p>Contains options related to the dimension colour:</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Auto</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Sets auto colour selection for each dimension. It is white if the background is dark and black if the background is light.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Custom</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Check this option to display all dimensions in user-defined colour. Press on the square next to the option to select the colour.</p>
<p class="sub-head">Text group</p>
<p>Contains options related to the dimension values:</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Above line</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span>D</span><span>imension value is always above and the dimension line and parallel to it.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>In line</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Dimension value is always within the dimension line (the line breaks where the value is) and parallel to it.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Horizontal</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Dimension value is always within the dimension line (the line breaks where the value is) and always horizontal.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Axis prefix</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Check this option to display the axis prefix before the value. For 1D dimensions axis prefixes are X, Y, and Z. For 2D &#160;dimensions axis prefixes are XY, YZ, and ZX. For 3D dimensions no axis prefix is displayed.</p>
<p class="Note"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: For Gap&amp;Flush measurements no axis prefix is available.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Decimal places</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Number of decimal digits for the numeric values. Default value is 4 digits.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Font</b></span> button</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Press this button to call the <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Font</b></span> dialog, from where the dimension values font name, font style, and font size can be changed.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="parameterstitle" id="p2">Anti-aliased slider</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" id="p2"><span style="font-weight:normal;">Check this option to make dimension lines and values anti-aliased.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle" id="p2">Snap to lines</p>
<p class="parameterdescription" id="p2"><span style="font-weight:normal;">Check this option to enable snap mode. If this mode is enabled when creating or moving 1D dimension it snaps to the closest parallel 1D dimension when close to it.</span></p>

